ADA clearance is important. We want accessible sidewalks. For that reason, a narrow sidewalk, which UCLA researchers have found tend to be more common in POC neighborhoods in LA than white neighborhoods. Narrow sidewalks that were designed before modern ideas of accessibility are pretty much gobbled up by this need for ADA clearance, which again is a good thing. The solution to me seems to be, well, if you need more space, you can expand the sidewalk. You can work with the transit agencies to build into the road, to take some space away from cars and give it to pedestrians and bus riders, which, again, city leadership in Los Angeles says they want to encourage that kind of behavior.
ADA净空高度很重要。我们需要无障碍人行道。出于这个原因，加州大学洛杉矶分校（UCLA）的研究人员发现，窄人行道在洛杉矶的有色人种社区比白人社区更常见。在现代无障碍理念出现之前设计的窄人行道几乎被这种对ADA净空的需求给吞噬了，这再次说明这是一件好事。在我看来，解决方案似乎是，如果你需要更多空间，你可以扩宽人行道。你可以与交通机构合作，向道路延伸，从汽车那里分流一些空间给行人和公交乘客，再次说明，洛杉矶的城市领导层表示他们希望鼓励这种行为。

53
00:25:54.000 --> 00:26:40.000
